{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$reviewText = @'\"'\nReviewed: 8877344ded4e2c53267b99fa2d047292347df003\n\nVerified: The prescribed 170 tests pass. Real-worktree entry-point tests exercise recorded Sol calls, work edits, sibling telemetry commits, pending logs, resumed Terra turns, detached concurrent calls, commit refusal and blackout refusal. I found no reachable major runtime failure in those flows. Independent probes confirmed that a readable branch claim suffices without a declared trunk and that resume selection orders the timestamp suffix, not the UUID-prefixed filename. Findings below concern requirement accuracy and the rubric's backlink rule. The worktree remained clean; no code was edited or committed.\n\nCommands:\n- \"'`git rev-parse HEAD` -> `8877344ded4e2c53267b99fa2d047292347df003`.\n- `git diff 4c418cd53b30d708fc40c37995b79da15757728e...8877344ded4e2c53267b99fa2d047292347df003 -- . '\"':(exclude)docs/iteration' ':(exclude)docs/reviews' ':(exclude)docs/log.md' ':(exclude)docs/log.d' ':(exclude)PROJECT_STATE.html' ':(exclude)docs/open-items.html' ':(exclude)docs/stage'\"'` (stat and scoped path reads), `Get-Content` and `rg` over the governing guide, PROCESS sections, rubric, WI/spec reference, changed implementation/tests/guidance, and cited registry rows -> reviewed the changed service boundary and its coordinator consumer; no parent SN/SR acceptance or approval change. Implementer session notes and self-assessments were not evidence.\n- With `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-21-leg11` and bytecode disabled: `C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -n 2 --basetemp C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-21-leg11/l12-r2a/wi-960 tests/test_codex_call.py tests/test_codex_call_git.py tests/test_session_service.py tests/test_prompts.py` -> `170 passed in 6